  "goodToKnow": "Der Leibwächter (die Leibwächterin) is a bodyguard. In official German, especially for the federal police (BKA) protecting politicians, the term is der Personenschützer. Der Leib is an elevated word for body: Leib und Seele (body and soul), mit Leib und Seele (wholeheartedly). Historically, rulers had a Leibgarde. The plural is the same."
